START

In the format-2 workstation layout the real command is tam-start. Before
displaying the interactive menu it completes the prepared system/settings
switch through the rootstock's bundle tool. It re-executes the selected
executable when the product version changes. Read-only queries retain their
normal behavior.

First text-login workstation activities menu (D215 / D224).

From 0.2.0 onward, start is a pure C program linked only against libtam (and
libc). It is not a Python script and must not regain a Python runtime
dependency. It works on systems without a Python interpreter.

The interactive TUI (pager) is separate from the menu catalog it displays.
Edit the catalog in <menu.json>; do not hard-code activities in C except for
id-specific launch helpers (Frotz story prompt, pMARS warriors).


BUILD

Requires an installed libtam (pkg-config libtam, or LIBTAM_PREFIX).

    make
    make check
    make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local/dev


INSTALL LAYOUT

  Path: $PREFIX/bin/start
  Content: Binary

  Path: $PREFIX/share/start/menu.json
  Content: Activity catalog

  Path: $PREFIX/share/start/VERSION
  Content: Command semver

  Path: $PREFIX/share/licenses/start/LICENSE
  Content: GPL-3.0-or-later

Optional overrides: START_MENU points at an alternate catalog file;
START_VERSION overrides the version string (checked before VERSION files).


USAGE

    start              # interactive menu (TTY required)
    start --list       # letter, id, command, installed, description
    start --check      # per-item install marks and N/M summary
    start --version|-V
    start --help|-h

The AI Agents section opens Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity CLI, OpenCode, and
Grok CLI using their normal commands on PATH. Entries show whether the command
is installed. The menu does not install agents or change their settings.

Opening the menu never starts graphics; the desktop launches only when the
user selects that activity. Quit with Esc (Backspace and Delete also quit).


LICENSE

GPL-3.0-or-later. See <LICENSE>.
